course: dictionary
lesson: 3211
title: Enlarge: making things bigger
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To enlarge something is to make it bigger. Enlarge is a verb, so it is an action: enlarge, enlarges, enlarged, enlarging. Look at the words around it to be sure. «Digital zoom just enlarges pixels and loses detail» tells you the pixels get bigger, and that the picture gets blurry.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Digital zoom just makes pixels bigger and loses detail» still makes sense, so you have it right. The clue «getting closer gives sharper pictures» shows that a bigger picture is not always a better one.
explain: Enlarge has special meanings in other subjects. In maths, to enlarge a shape is to make a similar shape with every side multiplied by the same number, called the scale factor. In science, a magnifying glass makes things look enlarged, so tiny things look bigger.
fact: To enlarge something means to make it bigger.
fact: «Enlarge a photo» means to print or show a bigger copy of it.
fact: In maths, «enlarge» a shape by a scale factor of 2 means every side is twice as long, and the angles stay the same.
fact: «Enlarged» can describe a body part too: a panda's «enlarged wrist bone» works like a thumb to grip bamboo.
fact: Enlarge is a verb: enlarge, enlarges, enlarged, enlarging.
exercise: «Digital zoom just enlarges pixels and loses detail.» What does enlarges mean here? | Makes brighter in colour | Makes colder | *Makes bigger | Makes quieter
exercise: Ava wants to enlarge a photo of her dog. What does she need to do? | Cut the dog out of it | Delete the photo | *Print or show a bigger copy of it | Make the photo quieter
exercise: A shape is enlarged by a scale factor of 2. What happens to its sides? | The sides stay exactly the same | Each side becomes half as long | *Each side becomes twice as long | The angles double
test: «Watch a panda eat and you will see an enlarged wrist bone that works like an extra thumb.» What does enlarged mean here? | Painted a bright colour | *Made bigger than usual | Hidden under the fur | Broken into pieces
test: Which word is closest in meaning to enlarge? | Freeze | Shrink | Hide | *Expand
exam: A magnifying glass lets a tiny ant look much bigger. Which word describes the ant through the glass? | *Enlarged | Erased | Painted | Shrunk
